# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local secrets (e.g. GOOGLE_ELEVATION_API_KEY)
.env

# NOTE: locations/ and figures/ are intentionally NOT ignored — they're
# already tracked in git history. See docs/issues/008-repo-hygiene.md for
# the open discussion about whether generated data belongs in git at all
# (Git LFS vs. regenerate-on-demand) before changing that.
#
# New generated outputs (friction_weighting.py and beyond), by contrast,
# start out ignored by default rather than repeating the same "large
# regenerable binary committed to git" pattern before that discussion is
# resolved. Regenerate locally with `python friction_weighting.py`.
locations/*/*_friction.graphml
